# What a language server should use for `src/`, and nothing else.
#
# Without this the Haxe extension has no classpath to work from, falls back to the workspace root,
# and reports two things that are not true of any real build:
#
#   `package hxscript.macro;` in src/hxscript/macro/Abstract.hx should be `package src.hxscript.macro;`
#   Type not found : hxscript.compile.Unsupported
#
# Both are the root being on the classpath instead of `src`. `extraParams.hxml` beside this file is
# not a substitute: it carries the setup macros applied to anyone using `-lib hxscript` and declares
# no classpath at all.
#
# The defines are here because half the library does not exist without them. `hxscript.cppia` and
# `hxscript.hl` are each behind their own, so a server given neither reports their contents missing.
# This one is the cppia side, which is hxcpp, which is the reference target. `completion-hl.hxml` is
# the other.
#
# Verified: `haxe completion.hxml --macro include('hxscript') --no-output` types every file under
# `src/` with no errors.

-cp src

-cpp bin_completion
-D hxscript_cppia
-D scriptable
